# gha-for-devops

Reusable GitHub Actions workflows for CI/CD, security, infrastructure, and developer automation.

[![CI](https://github.com/dceoy/gha-for-devops/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/dceoy/gha-for-devops/actions/workflows/ci.yml)

## Usage

Call a reusable workflow from a job in your repository:

```yaml
name: YAML lint
on:
  pull_request:

jobs:
  lint:
    uses: dceoy/gha-for-devops/.github/workflows/yaml-lint.yml@main
```

For production use, replace `@main` with a release tag or commit SHA. Pass sensitive values through `secrets:`, never `with:`. Cache-enabled workflows document options such as `enable-cache`, `cache-dependency-path`, and `cache-salt` in their workflow files.

### Weekly releases

The [CI workflow](.github/workflows/ci.yml) invokes the reusable [weekly release workflow](.github/workflows/weekly-release.yml) every Monday at 09:15 JST (00:15 UTC). It publishes only when a reusable workflow (a `.github/workflows/*.yml` or `*.yaml` file defining `workflow_call`) has changed since the latest stable SemVer release, including additions, deletions, or removal of `workflow_call`. Changes only to regular CI workflows, composite actions, shared scripts, the Actions lockfile, or documentation do not trigger a release. Otherwise, it validates the exact candidate commit with ShellCheck/shfmt, Markdown lint, GitHub Actions lint/security checks, and available Bats tests before publishing. This is independent of earlier `push` runs, which can be missing after token-driven merges.

Once reusable workflow changes trigger a release, version severity uses all first-parent commit messages since the previous release, including unrelated documentation, scripts, and ordinary CI changes. A `feat:` commit or squash-merge entry increments the minor version; other changes, including `chore(deps):`, increment the patch version. Breaking-change markers (`!:`, `BREAKING CHANGE:`, and `BREAKING-CHANGE:`) also increment the minor version instead of requiring a major release; the major component is unchanged by weekly automation. The release planning and publication logic is implemented directly in the reusable workflow, without a composite action or caller-local script. The workflow rejects non-`main` dispatches and conflicting release tags, and atomically creates the version tag at the validated commit before publishing a GitHub Release. If GitHub Release creation fails after tag creation, rerunning on the same commit can complete publication using that tag; tags at different objects are rejected. The `v1`-style major tag is synchronized after publication and reconciled to the latest published release on no-change runs, so failed tag synchronization can recover.

For an on-demand run, dispatch **CI/CD** on `main` with `workflow: weekly-release`. The existing tag-based manual release remains available.

### mise lockfile updates

Refresh `mise.lock` without installing project tools, and open a PR only when the lockfile or native dependency sidecars change:

```yaml
name: Refresh mise lock
on:
  schedule:
    - cron: "17 3 * * 1"
  workflow_dispatch:

jobs:
  update-mise-lock:
    permissions:
      contents: write
      pull-requests: write
    uses: dceoy/gha-for-devops/.github/workflows/mise-lock-update.yml@main
```

The workflow runs `mise lock --bump` by default, updating floating version requests within the constraints of `mise.toml` without changing that file. Exactly pinned versions remain pinned; update them separately (for example, with Renovate). Set `bump: false` to refresh lockfile metadata only. Use a dedicated `GH_TOKEN` (PAT or GitHub App token) if PRs need to trigger CI, because PRs made with the default `GITHUB_TOKEN` do not trigger other workflows.

### GitHub Pages

For a conventional Hugo site, call the combined build and deployment workflow:

```yaml
jobs:
  deploy:
    permissions:
      contents: read
      id-token: write
      pages: write
    uses: dceoy/gha-for-devops/.github/workflows/hugo-deploy-to-gh-pages.yml@main
```

For a custom build, upload a Pages artifact in one job and reuse only the deployment contract:

```yaml
jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      contents: read
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1
        with:
          persist-credentials: false
      - run: ./scripts/build-site.sh
      - uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@fc324d3547104276b827a68afc52ff2a11cc49c9 # v5.0.0
        with:
          path: public

  deploy:
    needs: build
    permissions:
      id-token: write
      pages: write
    uses: dceoy/gha-for-devops/.github/workflows/github-pages-deploy.yml@main
```

### Go quality checks

Keep generic correctness checks separate from linting and vulnerability analysis, and retain repository-specific validation in a local job:

```yaml
jobs:
  lint-and-scan:
    permissions:
      contents: read
      security-events: write
    uses: dceoy/gha-for-devops/.github/workflows/go-package-lint-and-scan.yml@main

  test:
    permissions:
      contents: read
    uses: dceoy/gha-for-devops/.github/workflows/go-package-test.yml@main
    with:
      race-enabled: true
      coverage-enabled: true
      upload-coverage: true

  validate-config:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      contents: read
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1
        with:
          persist-credentials: false
      - run: go run ./cmd/example validate ./config.yml
```

### GitHub Actions lint compatibility

`github-actions-lint-and-scan.yml` keeps actionlint enabled while ignoring the known v1.7.12 false positives for GitHub.com's `$/` self-repository syntax and the `job.workflow_ref`, `job.workflow_sha`, `job.workflow_repository`, and `job.workflow_file_path` properties (tracked in [actionlint#647](https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/issues/647), [actionlint#705](https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/issues/705), and [actionlint#711](https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/issues/711)). The built-in ignores apply only when `GITHUB_SERVER_URL` is `https://github.com`; GitHub Enterprise Server keeps raw diagnostics because `job.workflow_*` properties are unavailable there. Compatibility mode only suppresses actionlint diagnostics; it does not add `$/` support to older runners. Set `actionlint-compatibility-mode: false` to restore raw behavior. Use `actionlint-extra-ignore-regex` only for other narrow, temporary compatibility rules.

### Shell lint

Use `shell-lint.yml` for ShellCheck and optionally enable `shfmt` formatting checks:

```yaml
jobs:
  shell-lint:
    permissions:
      contents: read
    uses: dceoy/gha-for-devops/.github/workflows/shell-lint.yml@main
    with:
      use-shfmt: true
      shfmt-options: --indent=2 --binary-next-line --case-indent --space-redirects
```

